From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmscript: the script object loads a DMSC form and runs it in an ActiveScript engine (Init, CallRoutine, Set/GetVariable*, EnumRoutine/EnumVariable), AudioVBScript class

IDirectMusicScript was a set of stubs returning S_OK without doing
anything, and IPersistStream::Load only traced the file. It now behaves
as the DirectMusic documentation describes:

- Load reads the DMSC form (script header, language, source, GUID, version,
  name, category); E_POINTER without a stream, DMUS_E_SCRIPT_INVALID_FILE
  for another form or a form without header, language or source,
  DMUS_E_SCRIPT_LANGUAGE_INCOMPATIBLE when no engine exists for the
  language. "AudioVBScript" is served by the VBScript engine, and the
  AudioVBScript class itself now creates that engine instead of being
  CLASS_E_CLASSNOTAVAILABLE. The descriptor of a new object also has
  DMUS_OBJ_VERSION (0.0), as the conformance test says.
- Init(performance) parses and runs the global code of the script once;
  E_POINTER without performance, DMUS_E_NOT_INIT before Load, and a script
  or syntax error gives DMUS_E_SCRIPT_ERROR_IN_SCRIPT with the error
  information (hr, line, character, description, source line) filled in.
  Calls before Init return DMUS_E_NOT_INIT.
- CallRoutine runs a routine (DMUS_E_SCRIPT_ROUTINE_NOT_FOUND, or
  DMUS_E_SCRIPT_ERROR_IN_SCRIPT with the error information).
- SetVariableVariant / GetVariableVariant / SetVariableNumber /
  GetVariableNumber / SetVariableObject / GetVariableObject read and write
  the global variables of the script (DMUS_E_SCRIPT_VARIABLE_NOT_FOUND,
  DMUS_E_SCRIPT_UNSUPPORTED_VARTYPE, DMUS_E_SCRIPT_NOT_A_REFERENCE; an
  uninitialised variable reads as 0).
- EnumRoutine / EnumVariable list the routines and variables declared at
  the top level of the source in declaration order and return S_FALSE after
  the last. The engines that Wine ships cannot list their global names, so
  the declarations ("Sub", "Function", "Dim" and "function", "var") are read
  from the source text.

dmscript now imports oleaut32. Conformance test: the todo_wine mark on the
descriptor of an object with nothing loaded is removed.
Test: test/dmscript-gate.sh (+ dmscript-probe.c, dmscript-gate-common.sh).
